From d451169af2ba5ea5ecc001bbd57ecf80d4c7e886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:33:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 121/126] decode-link: pass the encryption of a VLESS link
 instead of refusing it

The parameter "encryption" of a link becomes the option of the outbound when it is a
setting Xray takes (mode, 1rtt or 0rtt, padding, keys of 32 or 1184 bytes), from the
parameter or by its path; another is refused. With it a flow is accepted over a
transport and without TLS, as Xray accepts it.
